# Next.js + React + TypeScript

## Component boundaries

- Default to Server Components for render-only/static UI.
- Add `"use client"` only when a component needs state, effects, event handlers, browser APIs, client-only context, or a client library.
- Keep the client boundary as low in the tree as practical.
- Do not convert a large route/page to a Client Component to support one small browser behavior if that behavior can be isolated safely.

## React

- Prefer simple functional components and composition.
- Avoid effects for values that can be derived during render.
- Effects must clean up subscriptions, timers, or listeners they create.
- Do not copy server/prop state into local state without a reason.
- Use stable keys based on data identity, not array indexes when items can change.
- Keep interaction state close to the interactive component.

## TypeScript

- Do not introduce `any`.
- When touching existing `any`, narrow it if the change can do so safely.
- Use `unknown` for caught/foreign values and narrow before property access.
- Define reusable domain types for portfolio projects, guestbook entries, and shared data.
- Prefer discriminated/string unions over unrestricted strings when a finite set exists.
- Avoid unsafe casts used only to silence the compiler.
- Keep types near their domain data unless a shared type module is clearly warranted.

## Next.js

- Use `next/link` for internal navigation.
- Use `next/image` for raster content images when optimization is beneficial; do not force it for icons/SVGs without reason.
- Use route/layout metadata APIs instead of ad-hoc document-head manipulation.
- Keep metadata and structured content truthful and synchronized with the actual site.
- Preserve App Router conventions.
- Check framework compatibility before changing Next.js/React versions or config.

## Data organization

- Do not duplicate factual portfolio content across multiple components/pages.
- Prefer one typed data source and derive featured/full views from it.
- Keep display-only JSX/icons outside raw factual data when that improves reuse.
